Trademarks and derivation. The image replaces Fedora's fedora-logos package
with generic-logos from the Fedora Project's repositories, as Fedora's
trademark guidelines ask of a system derived from Fedora; its RPM states its
licence as GPL-2.0-only AND LicenseRef-Callaway-LGPLv2+. The image also
replaces Bazzite's logo files with the Cairn mark and rewrites os-release to
name Cairn Linux. Until the boot screen and its initramfs are rebuilt, the
initial boot splash still carries Bazzite's artwork, a computer with no
hostname of its own is still called bazzite, and a computer that updated
from Bazzite keeps Bazzite's name in its boot menu. Fedora and the Infinity
design logo are trademarks of Red Hat, Inc. Bazzite's name and logo belong
to the Bazzite project. Apart from those leftovers, Cairn Linux uses neither
as its own name or mark. The licence of every package in the image is in
/usr/share/licenses.
